  "generated_text": "To solve this problem, we can use a recursive approach. Let $a_n$ be the number of $n$-digit numbers with two consecutive 1's. We can derive the following recurrence relation:\n\n$$a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}$$\n\nThis recurrence relation can be understood by considering the last digit of the number. If the last digit is 1, then the second last digit must be 1 as well, and the remaining $n-2$ digits can be any valid number. If the last digit is 2, then the remaining $n-1$ digits can be any valid number.\n\nWe can solve this recurrence relation using the initial conditions $a_1 = 1$ and $a_2 = 2$.\n\n$$a_1 = 1$$\n$$a_2 = 2$$\n$$a_3 = 3$$\n$$a_4 = 5$$\n$$a_5 = 8$$\n$$a_6 = 13$$\n$$a_7 = 21$$\n$$a_8 = 34$$\n$$a_9 = 55$$\n$$a_{10} = 8",
